      "sequence_position": 20,
      "problem": "$$\n\nFind the derivative of $t(x)=\\frac{\\operatorname{sinh}⁡x}{x}.$",
      "worked_solution": "In this case, the expression for $t(x)$ is a quotient $\\frac{u(x)}{v(x)}$ with $u(x)=\\operatorname{sinh}⁡x$ and $v(x)=x.$ \n\nTherefore, we apply the quotient rule as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}{t}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{{u}^{′}(x)\\cdot v(x)-u(x)\\cdot {v}^{′}(x)}{[v(x)]^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{(\\operatorname{sinh}⁡x)^{′}\\cdot x-\\operatorname{sinh}⁡x\\cdot (x)^{′}}{(x)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{x\\operatorname{cosh}⁡x-\\operatorname{sinh}⁡x}{{x}^{2}}\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
